---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const breadcrumbLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  'itemListElement': [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 1, 'name': 'Home', 'item': 'https://portfolioatlas.org' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', 'position': 2, 'name': 'Privacy Policy', 'item': 'https://portfolioatlas.org/privacy' },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How PortfolioAtlas handles your data: what stays in your browser, what our analytics collect, and how feedback and newsletter emails are used."
  jsonLd={breadcrumbLd}
>
  <div class="container-narrow py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-950 mb-6">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          PortfolioAtlas has no accounts, no logins, and no user database. Most of what you do
          here stays in your browser. This page explains exactly what we collect, why, and who
          processes it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Your calculator inputs stay in your browser</h2>
        <p>
          The numbers you enter - portfolio value, savings, passive income, retirement length,
          household size, healthcare costs - are processed entirely in your browser. They are
          kept in session storage so they follow you between pages, and they are erased when you
          close the tab. We do not transmit them to our servers, and we have no database that
          stores them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two things to be aware of. If you use a Share button, your inputs are encoded into the
          link you copy, so anyone you send that link to can see them. And our analytics receive
          a coarse range (for example "between $500K and $1M"), never the exact amount you typed.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used: which pages are visited
          and which features are used (for example, whether the comparison tool or a filter was
          used). Google sets cookies for this and processes the data under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>. We use this
          information to improve the site and to measure whether people find it useful.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can block analytics with standard browser tools (content blockers, or Google's own
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out add-on</a>) and the site
          works exactly the same.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">The feedback form</h2>
        <p>
          The feedback form asks for a message, and optionally your name and email. Your email is
          used for one thing: replying to you. It is relayed directly to our inbox (via Resend,
          an email delivery service) and is not stored in any site database, shared with anyone,
          or added to any mailing list. If you leave the email field blank, the feedback is
          anonymous.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">The newsletter</h2>
        <p>
          Our newsletter runs on Substack. When you subscribe, your email goes to Substack, not
          to this website, and is handled under
          <a href="https://substack.com/privacy">Substack's privacy policy</a>. Unsubscribing is
          available in every email Substack sends. We never add anyone to the newsletter
          ourselves - the only way onto the list is subscribing through Substack.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes standard technical data (such as IP
          addresses) to deliver pages and protect against abuse, as virtually every website host
          does.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Who your data touches</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> - analytics, as described above.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> - hosting and content delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> - relays feedback form submissions to our inbox.</li>
          <li><strong>Substack</strong> - runs the newsletter, entirely on their systems.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal data, run third-party ad trackers, or share your information
          with anyone beyond the services listed above.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          If you have emailed us feedback and want that email deleted, or want to know what we
          hold about you (for feedback, it is just the email thread itself), contact us at
          <a href="mailto:chris@portfolioatlas.org">chris@portfolioatlas.org</a> and we will sort
          it out. For newsletter data, use the unsubscribe link in any issue or contact Substack.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-brand-950 mt-12 mb-4">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how the site handles data, we will update this page. Material changes will
          be noted on the blog.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
          Published July 5, 2026. The practices described here have applied since PortfolioAtlas
          launched in March 2026 - this page documents them; it did not change them.
          PortfolioAtlas is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect
          their data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
